@baseUrl = http://localhost:3210

# ======================================================================
# AUTH
# ======================================================================

### Registrar usuário (público após @Public)
# @name register
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "matheus@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret"
}

### Login — captura o access_token pra reusar nas rotas protegidas
# repara: vem em .data.access_token por causa do TransformInterceptor ({ data: ... })
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "matheus@example.com",
  "password": "supersecret"
}

### Variável com o token capturado do login acima
@token = {{login.response.body.data.access_token}}

# ======================================================================
# PRODUCTS — happy path (rotas de escrita exigem Bearer)
# ======================================================================

### Criar produto (guarda a resposta como "create" pra reusar o id)
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "Mouse",
  "price": 99.9,
  "stock": 10
}

### Listar produtos 
GET {{baseUrl}}/products

### Buscar por id 
# o id vem em .data.id por causa do TransformInterceptor
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/{{create.response.body.data.id}}

### Atualizar (PATCH parcial — manda só o que muda)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/products/{{create.response.body.data.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "price": 79.9
}

### Deletar — presta atenção no status (204) e no body vazio
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/products/{{create.response.body.data.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ======================================================================
# PRODUCTS — casos de erro (Pipes + HttpExceptionFilter)
# ======================================================================

### Body inválido — ValidationPipe barra (400, whitelist/forbid)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "",
  "price": -5,
  "stock": 1.5,
  "campoProibido": "nao deveria passar"
}

### UUID malformado — ParseUUIDPipe barra (400)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/nao-e-uuid

### UUID válido mas inexistente — 404 (NotFoundException)
GET {{baseUrl}}/products/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

# ======================================================================
# AUTH — casos de erro
# ======================================================================

### Login com senha errada — 401 (mesma mensagem, anti-enumeration)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "matheus@example.com",
  "password": "senhaerrada"
}

### Login com email inexistente — 401 (mesma mensagem)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "naoexiste@example.com",
  "password": "qualquercoisa"
}

### Register com body inválido — 400 (email inválido, senha curta)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nao-e-email",
  "password": "123"
}

# ======================================================================
# GUARD GLOBAL — testes de proteção
# ======================================================================

### Escrita SEM token → deve dar 401 (guard global)
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "SemToken",
  "price": 10,
  "stock": 1
}

### Escrita com token GARBAGE → deve dar 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer token.invalido.aqui

{
  "name": "TokenLixo",
  "price": 10,
  "stock": 1
}

### test: get auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me

